      "proof_review": {
        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Full2.3 support in independent Section6 read: formal polynomial-operator model a, natural evaluation maps, the two explicit Witt representations and their Nijenhuis-Richardson module compatibility, basis induction through an invertible block-triangular matrix, and the nonzero polynomial-derivation test forcing b_n=0. The displayed shuffle identities give the bounded routine module checks and matrix entries. The proof is independent of the gauge-expansion2.1 and its iterative logarithm support. Coefficient uniqueness is universal for natural formulas across algebras/operators, as established in6.4; no assertion of linear independence after specializing to a single degenerate algebra/operator. The closed coefficient expression2.4 is conjectural and excluded."
      },
      "extra_source_paths": [
        "raw/sigma-2016-037-072/paper-053-source/sigma16-053.tex",
        "raw/sigma-2016-037-072/paper-053-source.zip"
      ],
      "statement_scope": "For each n>=1, the universal natural higher Koszul bracket Phi_f^(n+1) on every characteristic-zero commutative superalgebra has the author unique rational coefficient formula c1*rho1^n(f)+sum(i=2..n)c_i*rho1^(n-i)rho_i(f), where rho_i=[mu_i,-] and mu_i multiplies i+1 arguments, with all Koszul signs and shuffle conventions as defined. Uniqueness is universal, not after specializing to an individual A or f. No conjectural closed formula2.4 or noncommutative extension is selected.",
      "editorial_warning": "",
