      "countable_problem_unit": true,
      "root_admission_required": true,
      "source_boundary_note": "The complete original Theorem 2.3 statement and independent Section 6 author proof are supplied, with characteristic-zero superalgebra, shuffle/sign and Nijenhuis–Richardson definitions. The full polynomial-operator natural-bracket model, both positive-Witt representations, module compatibility, block-triangular basis induction and polynomial-derivation test eliminating the extra direction are bundled as one universal all-arity outcome. Coefficient uniqueness is universal over all algebras/operators, as in the author model, rather than after one fixed specialization. Gauge-expansion Theorem 2.1 and iterative-logarithm support are not needed by this proof; conjectural closed coefficients and noncommutative extensions are unselected. The original repeated first term in the representation-commutator expansion and x/t notation in the derivation test are retained unchanged; the following author expansion is also included.",
